# Position atoms: \%^ \%$ \%V \%# \%'m \%l \%c \%v.

=== \%^ matches only at the start of the file
ref:    pattern.txt */\%^*
quote:  Matches start of the file.
given:
  |a
  a
keys:   :%s/\%^a/X/<CR>
expect:
  |X
  a

=== \%^\_.\{-}\zs finds the first match in the file
ref:    pattern.txt */\%^*
quote:  For example, to find the first "VIM" in a file:
given:
  x VIM
  y V|IM
keys:   /\%^\_.\{-}\zsVIM<CR>
expect:
  x |VIM
  y VIM

=== \%$ matches only at the end of the file
ref:    pattern.txt */\%$*
quote:  Matches end of the file.
given:
  |a
  a
keys:   :%s/a\%$/X/<CR>
expect:
  a
  |X

=== finding the last match in the file with \%$
ref:    pattern.txt */\%$*
quote:  This one will find the last "VIM" in the file:
given:
  |VIM
  VIM x
  VIM y
keys:   /VIM\ze\(\(VIM\)\@!\_.\)*\%$<CR>
expect:
  VIM
  VIM x
  |VIM y

=== \%23l matches in one line
ref:    pattern.txt */\%l*
quote:  Matches in a specific line.
given:
  |a
  a
  a
keys:   :%s/\%2la/X/<CR>
expect:
  a
  |X
  a

=== \%<23l matches above a line
ref:    pattern.txt */\%l*
quote:  Matches above a specific line (lower line number).
given:
  |a
  a
  a
keys:   :%s/\%<3la/X/<CR>
expect:
  X
  |X
  a

=== \%>23l matches below a line
ref:    pattern.txt */\%l*
quote:  Matches below a specific line (higher line number).
given:
  |a
  a
  a
keys:   :%s/\%>1la/X/<CR>
expect:
  a
  X
  |X

=== \%.l matches in the cursor line
ref:    pattern.txt */\%l*
quote:  Matches at the cursor line.
given:
  a
  |b a
  a
keys:   /\%.la<CR>
expect:
  a
  b |a
  a

=== \%23c matches in a byte column
ref:    pattern.txt */\%c*
quote:  Matches in a specific column.
given:  |abcd
keys:   :s/\%3c./(&)/<CR>
expect: |ab(c)d

=== \%c counts bytes, not characters
ref:    pattern.txt */\%c*
quote:  Actually, the column is the byte number (thus it's not exactly right for multibyte characters).
given:  |éab
keys:   :s/\%3c./(&)/<CR>
expect: |é(a)b

=== \%>c and \%<c bound a column range
ref:    pattern.txt */\%c*
quote:  Note that "\%<46c" matches in column 45 when the "." matches a byte in column 44.
given:  |abcdef
keys:   :s/\%>2c.\%<5c/(&)/g<CR>
expect: |ab(c)def

=== \%23v matches in a virtual column
ref:    pattern.txt */\%v*
quote:  Matches in a specific virtual column.
given:  |	ab
keys:   :s/\%9v./(&)/<CR>
expect:
  	|(a)b

=== \%v never matches halfway through a tab
ref:    pattern.txt */\%v*
quote:  Note that some virtual column positions will never match, because they are halfway through a tab or other character that occupies more than one screen character.
given:  |	ab
keys:   :s/\%3v./(&)/e<CR>
expect: |	ab

=== ^.*\%17v matches up to a virtual column
ref:    pattern.txt */\%v*
quote:  To match the text up to column 17:
given:  |abcdefg
keys:   :s/^.*\%4v/(&)/<CR>
expect: |(abc)defg

=== \%# matches at the cursor
ref:    pattern.txt */\%#*
quote:  Matches with the cursor position.
given:  |x ab ab
keys:   wl:s/.\%#./(&)/<CR>
expect: |x (ab) ab

=== \%'m matches at a mark
ref:    pattern.txt */\%'m*
quote:  Matches with the position of mark m.
given:  ab|cd
keys:   ma0:s/\%'a./(&)/<CR>
expect: |ab(c)d

=== \%>'m matches after a mark
ref:    pattern.txt */\%'m*
quote:  Matches after the position of mark m.
given:  ab|cd
keys:   ma0:s/\%>'a./(&)/g<CR>
expect: |abc(d)

=== \%V matches inside the Visual area
ref:    pattern.txt */\%V*
quote:  Match inside the Visual area.
given:  |aaaaa
keys:   lvl<Esc>:s/\%Va/X/g<CR>
expect: |aXXaa

=== \%V uses the last Visual area after it ended
ref:    pattern.txt */\%V*
quote:  When Visual mode has already been stopped match in the area that |gv| would reselect.
given:  |aaaaa
keys:   lvl<Esc>0/\%Va<CR>
expect: a|aaaa

=== \%V at both ends keeps the match inside the area
ref:    pattern.txt */\%V*
quote:  To make sure the whole pattern is inside the Visual area put it at the start and just before the end of the pattern
given:  |foo bar foo bar
keys:   v6l<Esc>:s/\%Vfoo.*ba\%Vr/(&)/<CR>
expect: |(foo bar) foo bar

=== \%V limits a :s to a Visual block
ref:    change.txt *pattern-delimiter*
quote:  In Visual block mode, use |/\%V| in the pattern to have the substitute work in the block only.
given:
  |aaaa
  aaaa
keys:   l<C-v>jl:s/\%Va/X/g<CR>
expect:
  aXXa
  |aXXa

=== without \%V a Visual :s works on whole lines
ref:    change.txt *pattern-delimiter*
quote:  Otherwise it works on whole lines anyway.
given:
  |aaaa
  aaaa
keys:   l<C-v>jl:s/a/X/g<CR>
expect:
  XXXX
  |XXXX
